# Deploy — v0.1.4

Ships the Webflow redirect table (12 ported 301s in `_redirects`, static assets only). No migrations and the Sanity dataset is untouched, so no backup is needed and rollback is code-only.

## Deploy

- [x] **1.** Deploy. The guard runs first, the build regenerates `web/public/_redirects` from the config via `prebuild`, then Wrangler publishes Worker + assets.

```bash
npm run deploy
```

- [ ] **2.** Critical check: an old URL must answer with the new 301. Expect `HTTP/2 301` with `location: /c` — a 404 here means the redirects did not ship; stop and roll back.

```bash
curl -sI https://www.luxradiology.co.nz/confirm
```

- [x] **3.** Tag the release.

```bash
git tag -a v0.1.4 -m "Release 0.1.4 — port Webflow redirect table"
```

- [x] **4.** Push the tag.

```bash
git push origin v0.1.4
```

## If it goes wrong

-   **1.** Fully reversible: this release writes no data, so rolling back the deployment is the whole rollback.

- [ ] **2.** Roll back to the previously deployed version (Worker and assets together).

```bash
wrangler rollback --config wrangler.prod.jsonc
```
